**Pipeline expectations.** $R_0 \approx 40.77\ \mathrm m$ and $T_0 \approx 2.883\ \mathrm s$. With linear drag, C7 solves the ODE exactly; the landing time is found numerically, $T \approx 2.757\ \mathrm s$ and $R \approx 34.07\ \mathrm m$ (tolerance $0.05\ \mathrm m$). Units check throughout ($k$ in $\mathrm{s^{-1}}$). The figure draws both paths, and the slider for $\theta$ redraws them. Changing $k$ to $0$ must reproduce $R_0$.
